  "submitted_text": "Step 1: Square both sides of the equation to eliminate the square roots.\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2x}}{\\sqrt{3x-1}}\\right)^2 = \\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2\n\\]\nStep 2: Simplify the equation.\n\\[\n\\frac{2x}{3x-1} = \\frac{9}{4}\n\\]\nStep 3: Cross-multiply to clear the fraction.\n\\[\n8x = 9(3x-1)\n\\]\nStep 4: Distribute the 9 on the right side.\n\\[\n8x = 27x - 9\n\\]\nStep 5: Move all terms involving \\(x\\) to one side of the equation.\n\\[\n8x - 27x = -9\n\\]\nStep 6: Combine like terms.\n\\[\n-19x = -9\n\\]\nStep 7: Divide both sides by -19 to solve for \\(x\\).\n\\[\nx = \\frac{9}{19}\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{\\frac{9}{19}}",
